From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tcdent <tcdent@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:03:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/38] rust: fs: mutating inode operations

Add create, mkdir, symlink, unlink, rmdir, rename and setattr to
`inode::Operations`, each handed the directory the VFS locked and the
dentry it named, with the parent lock modelled as `Locked<_, WriteSem>`
that is not released on return. The creating operations return the new
inode and the callback instantiates the dentry with it; `mkdir` returns
null to the VFS to say the passed dentry is the one to use. `setattr`
runs `setattr_prepare` first and hands the request over as `SetAttr`,
an accessor view of `struct iattr`.

`FileSystem::READ_ONLY` replaces the unconditional `SB_RDONLY`: a file
system without mutating operations, like the sample, sets it.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SKmspe5nVbuvzdvYZa9UhW
